# Agent Skills Rules

## Scope

What this spoke covers:

- `SKILL.md` shape, frontmatter, and progressive disclosure
- Canonical published pack under `skills/<name>/`
- Dual-agent frontmatter (portable spec + Claude/Cursor extensions)

What this spoke does **not** cover (route elsewhere):

- `npx skills add` discovery and agent dirs → `skills-cli.mdc`
- Claude-only settings / additionalDirectories → `claude-code.mdc`
- Cursor personal vs project dirs → `cursor-skills.mdc`

## Invariants

1. Each published skill is `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. `name` in frontmatter
   matches the directory. No root `SKILL.md` (that stops `npx skills` from
   walking the pack unless `--full-depth`).
2. Portable frontmatter (required by the spec): `name`, `description`. Optional
   spec fields: `license`, `compatibility`, `metadata`, `allowed-tools`.
3. Superplan work-loop skills are **manual only**: set
   `disable-model-invocation: true` so they run when the user types `/name`.
4. Claude-only keys (`model`, `effort`, `argument-hint`) live in the same file;
   Cursor ignores unknown keys. Do not split into two SKILL.md files.
5. Keep `SKILL.md` under ~500 lines; move long reference into `references/`.
6. `.cursor/skills/` is this repo's build loop. `skills/` is what users install.
   Do not copy one tree into the other.
7. An empty pack (zero skill subdirectories) is valid. Git will not track that
   directory without a non-skill placeholder file. Pack-check must ignore files
   and only require `SKILL.md` inside subdirectories.

